<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madakari Nayaka V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1779</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madakari <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaka</a> V was the last of the Nayaka rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chitradurga">Chitradurga</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, reigning from 1758. He made shifting alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and others. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> of Mysore besieged his hill fort, which fell in 1779 after long resistance, and Madakari Nayaka died in captivity. He is a folk hero in Karnataka, as is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onake-obavva">Onake Obavva</a>, a woman celebrated for defending the fort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madakari-nayaka-v.jpg" alt="Madakari Nayaka V" width="238" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikhil0000711 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madakarinayaka_statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
